How about an Amulet of Identification, which allows the player to know certain
things about items he sees? Perhaps:

  cursed  - player gets wrong information (cursed->blessed, -2->+4, randomly
            decided so they're never sure if the info is true or not (as
            opposed to always telling the player the exact opposite of the
            truth, which would be easy to suss once you knew the amulet was
            cursed))

  normal  - lets player know blessed/cursed status

  blessed - lets player know blessed/cursed status, plusses/minuses and item
            type

These should be RARE and EXPENSIVE. They should drain food HEAVILY (or maybe
sap hitpoints?) to stop the game becoming too easy, and they should only
identify 1 item per turn in any case (to stop player getting hoard of stuff,
wearing amulet for 1 turn and doing an inventory, and then removing amulet
with whole inventory now identified).

Perhaps they should have some kind of limit on the number of items they can
identify; after this number of items has been identified, the amulet could
grow dull and not work any more (or, at least, not RELIABLY...)

Could make it a ring, I suppose, except that this way you'll have to take that
amulet of life saving _off_ to use this one... do you feel lucky, punk?

Comments? You could all think that this idea is a pile of dragon droppings, of
course - I've spent the whole afternoon implementing error recovery in a
compiler, so my brain is a little shot right now...

Oh yeah, while I'm at it, how about having some way of telling whether a
corpse is rotted or not? (Short of sacrificing or eating it, naturally...)

